Project tests and verification tools live here. Run the commands below from
src/test. Firmware build and upload scripts remain in src/python.

Native C++ tests
---------------
Install PlatformIO and a native C++ compiler (g++ on PATH). On Linux/macOS:

    export PYTHONPATH="$(pwd)/../python/external/esptool"
    export PLATFORMIO_BUILD_FLAGS="-DRegulatory_Domain_ISM_2400"
    pio test --project-dir .. -e native

On Windows PowerShell, use a current MinGW compiler and the packed-bitfield flag:

    $env:PYTHONPATH = (Resolve-Path ../python/external/esptool).Path
    $env:PLATFORMIO_BUILD_FLAGS = '-DRegulatory_Domain_ISM_2400 -mno-ms-bitfields'
    pio test --project-dir .. -e native

If the compiler is installed in this checkout's src/.pio/tools/mingw64/bin,
add it to the current process's PATH before running PlatformIO:

    $env:PATH = "$(Resolve-Path ../.pio/tools/mingw64/bin);$env:PATH"

Run both SRXL2 protocol and receiver-adapter tests together with:

    pio test --project-dir .. -e native -f test_srxl2

Python regression checks
------------------------
These scripts resolve repository paths relative to their own location:

    python test_serial_setup.py
    python test_srxl2_config.py
    python test_srxl2_platforms.py
    python -m unittest discover -s . -p 'test_*.py' -v

The first three checks compile and execute C++ probes. They use the checkout's
MinGW compiler when available, otherwise g++ on PATH. The configuration check
also needs ArduinoJson from an existing ESP32 receiver build in src/.pio/libdeps;
the platform check needs the installed Arduino ESP32 SDK in PLATFORMIO_CORE_DIR
(default: ~/.platformio). Image-provenance tests need src/hardware and use
synthetic firmware containers.

Frontend checks
---------------
Install the dependencies from src/html/package-lock.json with
`npm ci --prefix ../html`, then run:

    node test-serial-options.mjs
    node check-syntax.mjs
    node check-lint.mjs

The scripts resolve sources, configuration, and dependencies in src/html,
independently of the current directory. The same checks are available through
`npm --prefix ../html test`, `npm --prefix ../html run check:syntax`, and
`npm --prefix ../html run check:lint`.

Firmware and hardware tools
---------------------------
    python verify-er6-image.py /path/to/firmware.bin
    python verify-srxl2-production.py /path/to/firmware.elf [port] [nm-path]
    python power_sweep.py --help

The ER6 verifier requires a clean checkout matching the image's embedded source
revision and the pinned src/hardware revision. The production verifier defaults
to UART0 and the Windows ESP32 nm executable under ~/.platformio; pass port 1
for UART1 and the appropriate nm executable for other targets or operating systems.
The voltage sweep requires pyserial, the KoradSerial library
(https://github.com/starforgelabs/py-korad-serial), and connected receiver/power-supply
hardware. Its --help command runs without those hardware dependencies.

PlatformIO unit-testing documentation:
https://docs.platformio.org/page/plus/unit-testing.html
